<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-VENTER KEEPS FREE STATE ON TOP.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-VENTER KEEPS FREE STATE ON TOP.</headline>
<dateline>PAARL 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kosie Venter took four Boland</p>
<p>second innings wickets to add to his first innings half dozen to</p>
<p>put Free State on top in their four-day Supersport Series match</p>
<p>in Paarl on Sunday.</p>
<p>Venter finished the day with figures of four for 51 from 15</p>
<p>-- to add to his first innings six for 96 -- as Boland closed on</p>
<p>146 for five. On Monday they need a further 109 for victory with</p>
<p>five wickets in hand.</p>
<p>A see-sawing day began with Free State resuming on 98-1</p>
<p>which they took to 122-1 before five wickets fell for 33 runs to</p>
<p>four different bowlers and a run out.</p>
<p>A 71-run seventh wicket partnership between Hansie Cronje</p>
<p>(52) and Herman Bakkes (43) restored the Free State before they</p>
<p>were eventually bowled out for 264.</p>
<p>Boland lost Bryan Baguley to the seventh ball of the innings</p>
<p>and the introduction of off-spinner Venter worked immediately as</p>
<p>he took a wicket with his fourth ball and again bamboozled the</p>
<p>Boland batsmen with flight and spin.</p>
<p>However an unbroken sixth wicket partnership of 55 between</p>
<p>Adrian Kuiper (44 not out) and Andrew Wessels (30 not out)</p>
<p>offered Boland some hope.</p>
